WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:04.600
While plenty of Netflix originals have gotten
positive buzz over the last year, some of

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.220
them have flown under the radar without much
fanfare.

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:12.099
If you've already finished hits like Ozark,
The Crown and Narcos, then grab some popcorn,

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.660
settle in and check out these underrated Netflix
originals.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.480
Created by the showrunner of 2016’s Awkward,
coming of age series On My Block is equal

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:23.040
parts drama, comedy and political commentary.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:28.600
The series follows high school freshmen Monse,
Cesar, Jamal, and Ruben as they deal with

00:00:28.619 --> 00:00:32.680
a diverse range of challenges in their South
Central Los Angeles neighborhood, from teenage

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:37.200
confusion over romantic relationships to high-stakes
conflicts and gang violence.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:41.539
The potential for trouble and the distant
sound of gunshots might always be present

00:00:41.539 --> 00:00:45.930
in the backdrop of their neighborhood, but
thanks to its knack for empathetic storytelling

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:50.830
and the authentic performances of its talented
cast, On My Block never begins to feel like

00:00:50.830 --> 00:00:51.980
an after-school special.

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:56.900
A touch of dark humor and the occasional tender
moment between the characters manages to balance

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:58.500
the heavy subject matter, too.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:02.920
With young actors of color cast in the leading
roles and a storyline that weaves every plot

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:07.620
together without ever resorting to filler
episodes, On My Block offers a deeply effective

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:09.520
insight into life in the inner city.

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:15.000
While Stranger Things took a nostalgic look
back at the '80s, Everything Sucks! was inspired

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:19.720
by the teen comedy tropes which grew out of
the following decade, so if you consider yourself

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:24.320
a '90s kid, you might be able to relate to
the struggle of high school misfits like Kate,

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:26.700
Luke, McQuaid, Tyler, and Emaline.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:29.800
“What kind of fairy tale world does Alanis
Morissette live in?"

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:31.120
"Canada"

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:31.620
"Oh"

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:33.040
"Can I have a chip?"

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:33.540
"Oh, yeah.”

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:39.780
Set in the real, aptly-named small town of
Boring, Oregon in 1996, Everything Sucks!

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:43.790
follows a group of outcasts in the A/V and
drama clubs who decide to make a movie together

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:45.400
after the school play is canceled.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:50.420
Meanwhile, Luke struggles with his relationship
with his estranged father, Kate slowly comes

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:54.560
out to her friends and family, and Tyler finds
himself wondering why he can't seem to land

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:55.060
a date.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:02:00.740
The series stars several fresh faces, including
Jahi Winston as Luke and Quinn Liebling as

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:04.280
Tyler, alongside more familiar names like
Sydney Sweeney as Emaline.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:10.080
With a realistic storyline, a heaping of '90s
cultural references and a charming cast, Everything

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.400
Sucks! makes for something of a single-season
gem.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:18.880
Set on a remote Welsh island in 1905, the
terrifying period drama Apostle follows Thomas

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:23.160
Richardson as he attempts to rescue his sister
Jennifer from a secretive religious cult.

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:27.380
In order to pry some secrets out of cult members
who might be willing to reveal more than they

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:32.240
should, Thomas disguises himself as a curious
convert and eventually finds out that Jennifer

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:33.660
is being held for ransom.

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:38.360
From there, a gruesome battle for the future
of the island ensues, and if you get a bit

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:41.830
squeamish at the sight of blood, well, you
may want to keep your eyes shut.

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:46.730
But while Apostle might be gory, it's not
for mere shock value, the film is a bona fide

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:49.140
psychological thriller all the way through.

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:52.040
“This place this community it's broken."

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:53.180
"Then we’ll fix it!”

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:58.270
The fascinating mythology built around the
cult explores the dark side of the divine

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:02.980
feminine, and the open-ended conclusion will
at once satisfy viewers and leave them pondering.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:07.880
Kiss Me First is an experimental series which
alternates between the real and the surreal

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:10.620
as it flips from live action to virtual reality.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:16.430
Leila is a lonely teenager who spends most
of her days playing the MMORPG Azana, in which

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:20.100
she meets a more confident girl named Tess
who pulls her out of her shell.

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:24.960
The two eventually become close offline, but
when Tess disappears, Leila takes it upon

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:30.040
herself to solve the mystery and quickly learns
that virtual actions can have real world consequences.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:35.250
The series is based on the Lottie Moggach
novel of the same title, and with Skins creator

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:39.440
Bryan Elsley at the helm, you just know you're
in for plenty of juicy drama.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:40.840
“You’re not supposed to be cruel."

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:42.800
"I'm not.

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:46.760
I'm your friend and I’m here.”

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:52.040
Kiss Me First has echoes of Black Mirror,
another sci-fi series which explored the pitfalls

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:58.020
of human reliance on technology, and its uncanny
valley style of CGI makes it hard not to question

00:03:58.020 --> 00:03:59.880
your own relationship to your screens.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:02.480
You might want to spend a little time outside
after this one.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:08.960
Based on the novel Cornelia by Florencia Etcheves,
Perdida is a solid thriller that begins by

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:14.140
inviting the viewer into a setting that establishes
a genuine sense of impending doom, and then

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:17.860
establishes a tone which never quite lets
up throughout the rest of the film.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:23.040
Pipa, a policewoman whose friend Cornelia
went missing in Patagonia as a teenager, feels

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:27.000
like she can't find peace until she solves
the mystery behind her disappearance.

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:31.320
But as she sets out to discover what really
happened to her friend on that fateful day,

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:34.300
she realizes that the search might be putting
her own life in danger.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:38.960
Although the plot can drag a bit during the
scenes in which Pipa is engrossed in paperwork,

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.740
you’ll still remain gripped until the very
last moment.

